This is a Whitespace program that prints "مرحبا بالعالم" (Hello, World! in Arabic)
Whitespace is an esoteric programming language where only spaces, tabs, and linefeeds matter.
All other characters (like this text) are ignored by the interpreter.

The program uses:
- Space Space = Push number onto stack
- Tab Line-feed Space Space = Output character from stack
- Line-feed Line-feed = End program

Arabic text "مرحبا بالعالم" in UTF-8:
م = 0xD985 (55685)
ر = 0xD8B1 (55473)
ح = 0xD8AD (55469)
ب = 0xD8A8 (55464)
ا = 0xD8A7 (55463)
(space) = 0x20 (32)
ب = 0xD8A8 (55464)
ا = 0xD8A7 (55463)
ل = 0xD984 (55684)
ع = 0xD8B9 (55481)
ا = 0xD8A7 (55463)
ل = 0xD984 (55684)
م = 0xD985 (55685)

